Ongoing monitoring and risk management of each asset is conducted by the Adviser's portfolio management team under the supervision of the Chief Risk Officer. The portfolio management team is separate and distinct from the Adviser's investment team. The primary responsibilities of the portfolio management team are to:
•formally monitor portfolio companies post-investment on an ongoing basis;
•perform quarterly valuations of all assets in partnership with third-party valuation agent(s);
•maintain and update internal and external asset ratings;
•oversee BDC-level monitoring;
•lead amendment, “work out,” and restructurings processes
